# Server Conventions

- Server Actions: one domain file under `actions/` — no barrel re-exports. Shared helpers live in `actions/shared.ts`.
- Authorize before mutating (`assertProjectPermission`, `requireOnActive`, `requireOnFindingProject`).
- User-facing failures: throw `PublicError`. Unexpected errors: `reportError` / `reportWarning` from `observability.ts`.
- Evidence is insert-only — never UPDATE/DELETE evidence rows (DB trigger enforces this).
- Status changes go through core helpers (`advanceRemediation`, requirement-status transitions) — actions must not invent statuses.
- Never log or return raw GitHub tokens. Source trees are ephemeral temp clones (`repo-checkout.ts`).
- Long assessments: durable jobs + worker (`assessment-jobs`, `assessment-worker`), not long-running request handlers — no exceptions. `runAssessmentAction` only enqueues and schedules the drain in `after()`; the scan always runs in the worker route (or inline on the dev/e2e path). The rule forbids *new* long-running request handlers.
- Webhook deliveries are idempotent by `x-github-delivery`.

## Verification loop

- During work: `npx vitest run <touched-file>` (targeted, fast).
- At gate: `npm run verify:gate` (lint + typecheck + test + build); add `npm run test:db` when persistence changed, `npm run test:e2e` when routes/auth changed.
